STORY OF THYROID CANCER is listed as a major risk factor. In parallel, thyroid cancers are also described as often sporadic (no clear cause/risk factor), indicating risk can be genetic or absent/unknown in many cases. [Data: Entities (4972, 4998, 4983, 4956); Relationships (10935, 10991, 10939)]\\n\\nOLDER ADULTS are described as more susceptible to harsh side effects from cancer treatments, and radiation therapy is noted as more likely to damage the nervous system than chemotherapy, especially in older adults. This places age-related vulnerability as an important safety and planning consideration when radiation is being considered. [Data: Entities (4281); Relationships (8949)]\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"summary\": \"Care delivery considerations include procedural sedation for comfort and recovery/hospitalization after major surgery\",\n      \"explanation\": \"SEDATION is presented as medication-assisted calming or reduced awareness used to improve comfort during invasive procedures (including examples such as bedside bone marrow aspirate/biopsy and core needle biopsy), and the care team may provide sedation during procedures in some places to improve comfort. This reflects a practical, patient-centered support element that can affect procedural tolerance and experience. [Data: Entities (2961); Relationships (5640)]\\n\\nRECOVERY is described as variable by procedure intensity, with more extensive operations (e.g., radical cystectomy) often requiring longer recovery (2–3 months or more) and potentially a hospital stay ranging from several days to weeks depending on complexity and individual circumstances. This highlights how surgical choice can have substantial downstream operational impact for patients and facilities. [Data: Entities (2200); Relationships (3798)]\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"rating\": 3.6,\n  \"rating_explanation\": \"Impact is low-to-moderate because the community describes standard medical oncology concepts and care pathways with meaningful clinical signi